  "question": {
    "text": "A weightless rod of length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>l</mi></math> carries two equal masses&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math> one fixed at the end and other in the middle of the rod. The rod can revolve in a vertical plane about <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>. Then horizontal velocity which must be imparted to end&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> of the rod to deflect it to the horizontal position is<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/WhatsApp_Image_2020-07-27_at_3.14.48_PM.jpeg\" style=\"width: 180px; height: 194px;\" />",
